                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "================\nCODE SNIPPETS\n================\n### API Documentation for skipNodeModulesBundle option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nPrevents bundling of `node_modules`. Defaults to `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nskipNodeModulesBundle?: boolean\n  Defined in: types.ts:222\n  Description: Skip bundling node_modules.\n```\n\n```ts\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for report option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nEnables size reporting after bundling. Defaults to `true`.\n\n```APIDOC\nreport?: boolean | ReportOptions\n  Defined in: types.ts:267\n  Description: Enable size reporting after bundling.\n```\n\n```ts\ntrue\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configure Sourcemap Generation (sourcemap)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nAn optional setting to configure sourcemap generation for the bundled output. The default value is `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nsourcemap?: Sourcemap\nDefault: false\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for publint option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nEnables running publint after bundling. Requires `publint` to be installed. Defaults to `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\npublint?: boolean | Options\n  Defined in: types.ts:252\n  Description: Run publint after bundling. Requires publint to be installed.\n```\n\n```ts\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for tsconfig option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nConfigures the TypeScript configuration file to use.\n\n```APIDOC\ntsconfig?: string | boolean\n  Defined in: types.ts:83\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Initialize tsdown Configuration File\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/guide/getting-started.md\n\nThis `tsdown.config.ts` file defines the configuration for the `tsdown` bundler. It uses `defineConfig` to specify the entry point for the bundling process, which in this case is the `src` directory.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'tsdown'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  entry: ['./src'],\n})\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for plugins option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nConfigures plugins for the build process.\n\n```APIDOC\nplugins?: RolldownPluginOption<any>\n  Defined in: types.ts:189\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configuring Plugins in tsdown\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/advanced/plugins.md\n\nThis example illustrates how to add plugins to your tsdown configuration file. Plugins are specified within the 'plugins' array in the 'defineConfig' function, enabling their functionality during the bundling process.\n\n```ts\nimport SomePlugin from 'some-plugin'\nimport { defineConfig } from 'tsdown'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [SomePlugin()],\n})\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Skip Bundling Node Modules (skipNodeModulesBundle)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nAn optional boolean flag to prevent bundling of `node_modules` dependencies. The default value is `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nskipNodeModulesBundle?: boolean\nDescription: Skip bundling 'node_modules'.\nDefault: false\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for shims option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nConfigures shims. Defaults to `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nshims?: boolean\n  Defined in: types.ts:159\n```\n\n```ts\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Options Interface Property: bundle\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nDeprecated optional bundle property. Use `unbundle` instead. Type: boolean. Defaults to true.\n\n```APIDOC\nbundle?: boolean\nDeprecated: Use `unbundle` instead.\nDefault: true\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for sourcemap option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nConfigures sourcemap generation. Defaults to `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nsourcemap?: Sourcemap\n  Defined in: types.ts:110\n```\n\n```ts\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Enable Bundle Size Reporting (report)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nControls whether size reporting is enabled after the bundling process. The default value is `true`.\n\n```APIDOC\nreport?: boolean | ReportOptions\nDescription: Enable size reporting after bundling.\nDefault: true\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Integrate Configuration from Vite/Vitest (fromVite)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nEnables reusing configuration settings from Vite or Vitest. This feature is experimental.\n\n```APIDOC\nfromVite: boolean | \"vitest\"\nDescription: Reuse config from Vite or Vitest (experimental).\nDefault: false\n```\n\n```ts\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configure tsdown to force bundle specific dependencies\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/options/dependencies.md\n\nThis example shows how to use the `noExternal` option in `tsdown.config.ts` to explicitly force `some-package` to be bundled into the library, overriding the default externalization behavior.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'tsdown'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  noExternal: ['some-package'],\n})\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Reuse Configuration from Vite or Vitest\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nEnables the reuse of configuration settings from Vite or Vitest. This feature is experimental.\n\n```APIDOC\nfromVite?: boolean | \"vitest\"\nDefined in: types.ts:228\n```\n\n```ts\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Customize tsdown Bundling Platform\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/options/platform.md\n\nDemonstrates the basic usage of the `tsdown --platform` command to set the target runtime environment for bundled JavaScript, allowing selection among `node` (default), `browser`, or `neutral` targets.\n\n```bash\ntsdown --platform node    # default\ntsdown --platform browser\ntsdown --platform neutral\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Options.attw Property\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nOptional setting to run `arethetypeswrong` after bundling. Requires `@arethetypeswrong/core` to be installed. Defaults to `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nattw?: boolean | AttwOptions\n\nDefault:\nfalse\n\nSee: https://github.com/arethetypeswrong/arethetypeswrong.github.io\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Enable Unbundle Mode in tsdown Configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/options/unbundle.md\n\nThis snippet demonstrates how to configure `tsdown` to enable unbundle mode by setting the `unbundle` option to `true` within the `defineConfig` function. This ensures that `tsdown` processes files individually rather than bundling them.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'tsdown'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  entry: ['src/index.ts'],\n  unbundle: true,\n})\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for publicDir option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nAlias for `copy`, will be removed in the future. Configures the public directory copy options.\n\n```APIDOC\npublicDir?: CopyOptions | CopyOptionsFn\n  Defined in: types.ts:292\n  Deprecated: Alias for copy, will be removed in the future.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configure unused dependencies check\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nDocuments the 'unused' configuration option. This option enables checking for unused dependencies and can be a boolean or an Options object. It requires the 'unplugin-unused' package to be installed for functionality.\n\n```APIDOC\nProperty: unused\nType: boolean | Options\nDescription: Enable unused dependencies check with `unplugin-unused`.\nRequires `unplugin-unused` to be installed.\n```\n\n```TypeScript\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Options Interface Property: attw\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nOptional attw property to run `arethetypeswrong` after bundling. Requires `@arethetypeswrong/core`. Type: boolean | AttwOptions. Defaults to false.\n\n```APIDOC\nattw?: boolean | AttwOptions\nDefault: false\nSee: https://github.com/arethetypeswrong/arethetypeswrong.github.io\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Options.external Property\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nOptional external dependency configuration.\n\n```APIDOC\nexternal?: ExternalOption\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Enable Publint Integration (publint)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nDetermines whether to run `publint` after bundling to check package integrity. Requires `publint` to be installed. The default value is `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\npublint?: boolean | Options\nDescription: Run publint after bundling. Requires 'publint' to be installed.\nDefault: false\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configure tsdown to externalize specific dependencies\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/options/dependencies.md\n\nThis example demonstrates how to use the `external` option in `tsdown.config.ts` to prevent `lodash` and all packages under the `@my-scope` namespace from being bundled, treating them as external dependencies.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'tsdown'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  external: ['lodash', /^@my-scope\\//],\n})\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Set Output Directory\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nDefines the directory where the bundled output files will be placed.\n\n```APIDOC\noutDir?: string\nDefined in: types.ts:108\n```\n\n```ts\n'dist'\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Specify Output Directory (outDir)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nSets the directory where the bundled output files will be placed.\n\n```APIDOC\noutDir: string\nDescription: Sets the directory where the bundled output files will be placed.\nDefault: 'dist'\n```\n\n```ts\n'dist'\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Example tsdown Platform Configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/options/platform.md\n\nProvides practical examples of using the `tsdown --platform` command to bundle code specifically for Node.js, web browsers, or a platform-agnostic (neutral) environment, illustrating each command's effect.\n\n```bash\n# Bundle for Node.js (default)\ntsdown --platform node\n\n# Bundle for browsers\ntsdown --platform browser\n\n# Bundle for a neutral platform\ntsdown --platform neutral\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Run tsdown to Bundle Code\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/guide/getting-started.md\n\nThis command executes the `tsdown` bundler to process the source files according to the configuration. It compiles and bundles the TypeScript code, typically outputting the result to the `dist` directory.\n\n```sh\n./node_modules/.bin/tsdown\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Workspace Interface API Definition\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/workspace.md\n\nDefines the structure and properties of the `Workspace` interface, used for configuring workspace settings in tsdown. It includes optional properties for specifying a config file, directories to exclude, and directories to include.\n\n```APIDOC\nInterface: Workspace\n  Properties:\n    config?: string | boolean\n      Description: Path to the workspace configuration file.\n    exclude?: Arrayable<string>\n      Description: Exclude directories from workspace. Defaults to all node_modules, dist, test, tests, temp, and tmp directories.\n    include?: Arrayable<string>\n      Description: Workspace directories. Glob patterns are supported.\n        - auto: Automatically detect package.json files in the workspace.\n      Default: 'auto'\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configure Public Directory Copying (publicDir)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nAn optional alias for the `copy` option, used to configure copying of public directory assets. This option is deprecated and will be removed in future versions.\n\n```APIDOC\npublicDir?: CopyOptions | CopyOptionsFn\nDeprecated: Alias for 'copy', will be removed in the future.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Define Multiple Entry Files in tsdown.config.ts\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/options/entry.md\n\nThis snippet shows how to define multiple entry files using an array of strings within the \"tsdown\" configuration. Each string in the array represents a separate entry point for the bundling process.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'tsdown'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  entry: ['src/entry1.ts', 'src/entry2.t