                          "text": "================\nCODE SNIPPETS\n================\n### Define Build Process Hooks (hooks)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nAllows defining custom hooks to interact with the build process. Can be a partial TsdownHooks object or a function that returns an Awaitable void.\n\n```APIDOC\nhooks: Partial<TsdownHooks> | (hooks) => Awaitable<void>\nDescription: Allows defining custom hooks to interact with the build process.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Execute Command After Successful Build (onSuccess)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nAllows specifying a command or function to be executed after a successful build, especially useful for Watch mode.\n\n```APIDOC\nonSuccess: string | (config, signal) => void | Promise<void>\nDescription: You can specify command to be executed after a successful build, specially useful for Watch mode\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Run tsdown Build Script via npm\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/guide/getting-started.md\n\nThis command executes the `build` script defined in `package.json`, which in turn runs `tsdown`. It provides a convenient and standardized way to trigger the bundling process within a project.\n\n```sh\nnpm run build\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Execute Command on Successful Build\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nSpecifies a command or function to be executed after a successful build, especially useful in watch mode.\n\n```APIDOC\nonSuccess?: string | (config, signal) => void | Promise<void>\nDefined in: types.ts:214\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Setup CommonJS Require and Export Resolve Function\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/tests/__snapshots__/node-protocol/with-require-polyfill-and-nodeProtocol-strip.snap.md\n\nThis JavaScript snippet demonstrates how to create a CommonJS `require` function in an ES module environment using Node.js's `createRequire`. It then exports the `resolve` method of this `require` function, allowing other modules to programmatically resolve module paths, often used in build tools or bundlers like Rolldown.\n\n```js\nimport { createRequire } from \"module\";\n\n//#region rolldown:runtime\nvar __require = /* @__PURE__ */ createRequire(import.meta.url);\n\n//#endregion\n//#region index.ts\nconst fn = __require.resolve;\n\n//#endregion\nexport { fn };\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Load Node.js Built-in Modules Asynchronously (JavaScript)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/tests/__snapshots__/node-protocol/dynamic-imports-with-nodeProtocol-true.snap.md\n\nThis JavaScript function, `loadBuiltins`, asynchronously imports and returns Node.js built-in modules `fs` and `path`. It's designed to provide access to these core functionalities within a project, ensuring they are loaded only when needed. The function returns an object containing the imported modules.\n\n```js\n//#region index.ts\nasync function loadBuiltins() {\n\tconst fs = await import(\"node:fs\");\n\tconst path = await import(\"node:path\");\n\treturn {\n\t\tfs,\n\t\tpath\n\t};\n}\n\n//#endregion\nexport { loadBuiltins };\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Skip Bundling Node Modules (skipNodeModulesBundle)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nAn optional boolean flag to prevent bundling of `node_modules` dependencies. The default value is `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nskipNodeModulesBundle?: boolean\nDescription: Skip bundling 'node_modules'.\nDefault: false\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Build with tsdown Programmatically\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/advanced/programmatic-usage.md\n\nDemonstrates how to use the `build` function from `tsdown` in a TypeScript environment. This example configures entry points, output formats (ESM and CJS), an output directory, and enables declaration file generation.\n\n```TypeScript\nimport { build } from 'tsdown'\n\nawait build({\n  entry: ['src/index.ts'],\n  format: ['esm', 'cjs'],\n  outDir: 'dist',\n  dts: true,\n  // ...any other options\n})\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Specify Target Platform for tsdown Bundling\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/options/platform.md\n\nDemonstrates how to use the `--platform` option with the `tsdown` command-line tool to specify the target runtime environment for the bundled JavaScript code. Options include `node` (default for Node.js and compatible environments), `browser` (for web browsers), and `neutral` (for platform-agnostic builds).\n\n```bash\n# 针对 Node.js 打包（默认）\ntsdown --platform node\n\n# 针对浏览器打包\ntsdown --platform browser\n\n# 针对中立平台打包\ntsdown --platform neutral\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Install: Inline Runtime Helpers (Development)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/options/target.md\n\nInstall `@oxc-project/runtime` as a development dependency if you prefer to inline helper functions directly into your bundled code instead of importing them from the runtime package.\n\n```bash\nnpm install -D @oxc-project/runtime\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Create an IIFE JavaScript Module\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/tests/__snapshots__/iife-and-umd.snap.md\n\nThis snippet demonstrates how to create an Immediately Invoked Function Expression (IIFE) module in JavaScript. It encapsulates variables and exports them to a global `Lib` object, preventing global scope pollution. This pattern is common for browser environments where modules are not natively supported.\n\n```JavaScript\nvar Lib = (function(exports) {\n\n\n//#region index.ts\nconst foo = true;\n\n//#endregion\nexports.foo = foo;\nreturn exports;\n})({});\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for skipNodeModulesBundle option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nPrevents bundling of `node_modules`. Defaults to `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nskipNodeModulesBundle?: boolean\n  Defined in: types.ts:222\n  Description: Skip bundling node_modules.\n```\n\n```ts\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Define Tsdown Hooks\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nAllows defining custom hooks to interact with the tsdown build process. Can be a partial `TsdownHooks` object or a function that receives hooks and returns an Awaitable void.\n\n```APIDOC\nhooks?: Partial<TsdownHooks> | (hooks) => Awaitable<void>\nDefined in: types.ts:306\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for publint option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nEnables running publint after bundling. Requires `publint` to be installed. Defaults to `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\npublint?: boolean | Options\n  Defined in: types.ts:252\n  Description: Run publint after bundling. Requires publint to be installed.\n```\n\n```ts\nfalse\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Enable Bundle Size Reporting (report)\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nControls whether size reporting is enabled after the bundling process. The default value is `true`.\n\n```APIDOC\nreport?: boolean | ReportOptions\nDescription: Enable size reporting after bundling.\nDefault: true\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Options.attw Property\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nOptional setting to run `arethetypeswrong` after bundling. Requires `@arethetypeswrong/core` to be installed. Defaults to `false`.\n\n```APIDOC\nattw?: boolean | AttwOptions\n\nDefault:\nfalse\n\nSee: https://github.com/arethetypeswrong/arethetypeswrong.github.io\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configure tsdown Build Script in package.json\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/guide/getting-started.md\n\nThis `package.json` snippet demonstrates how to add a `build` script that invokes `tsdown`. This simplifies the build process, allowing developers to run `npm run build` instead of typing the full CLI command.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-tsdown-project\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsdown\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"tsdown\": \"^0.9.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configure tsdown to force bundle specific dependencies\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/options/dependencies.md\n\nThis example shows how to use the `noExternal` option in `tsdown.config.ts` to explicitly force `some-package` to be bundled into the library, overriding the default externalization behavior.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'tsdown'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  noExternal: ['some-package'],\n})\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### API Documentation for report option\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/config-options.md\n\nEnables size reporting after bundling. Defaults to `true`.\n\n```APIDOC\nreport?: boolean | ReportOptions\n  Defined in: types.ts:267\n  Description: Enable size reporting after bundling.\n```\n\n```ts\ntrue\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Define Bundle Output Format\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/cli.md\n\nSpecifies the module format for the output bundle. Supported formats include `esm` (ECMAScript Modules), `cjs` (CommonJS), and `iife` (Immediately Invoked Function Expression).\n\n```bash\ntsdown --format esm\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Specify Output Directory\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/reference/cli.md\n\nCustomizes the output directory where the bundled files will be written. Use this option to control the build artifact location.\n\n```bash\ntsdown -d dist\ntsdown --out-dir build\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Options Interface Property: bundle\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/zh-CN/reference/config-options.md\n\nDeprecated optional bundle property. Use `unbundle` instead. Type: boolean. Defaults to true.\n\n```APIDOC\nbundle?: boolean\nDeprecated: Use `unbundle` instead.\nDefault: true\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Execute Bundled tsdown Output\n\nSource: https://github.com/rolldown/tsdown/blob/main/docs/guide/getting-started.md\n\nThis command runs the JavaScript file generated by `tsdown` after bundling. It verifies the successful compilation and execution of the bundled code, demonstrating that the `tsdown` process worked as expected.\n\n```sh\nnode dist/index.mjs\n```"
